# Documentation truthfulness

- Use only verified repository facts. Mark unknowns explicitly as UNKNOWN.
- Never invent test results, metrics, endpoints, or capabilities.
- Fix named acceptance criteria before implementation; report accepted/total with a stable
  denominator and explain scope changes. Keep implemented, integrated, deployed and live
  acceptance separate, with exact revisions, evidence and explicit unknown/unexecuted checks.
- A merge does not prove deployment; deployment does not prove a real user journey passed.
  Reuse evidence only when its relevant inputs still cover the candidate.
- Keep docs consistent with actual behavior; update docs when behavior/config changes.
- Do not overstate capability (no "autonomous", "guaranteed", or live-trading claims).
